00:36:17,820 --> 00:36:22,900
And it is like you guys are saying that, that sort of, you know, flash moment and you see it.

634
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:26,940
Sometimes it comes a little bit sooner and sometimes it comes a little bit later.

635
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:31,600
And I was talking to a friend the other day, we actually ended up, we actually ended up recording it.

636
00:36:31,680 --> 00:36:44,200
So I think we'll probably put out some shorts or something like that a little bit later, but it was just a really good authentic conversation with somebody who's newer to hacking, but has a high propensity, has that, that clearly has that mentality, right?

637
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:44,700
For hacking.

638
00:36:45,140 --> 00:36:51,600
And he's already found a bunch of bugs, you know, in a, in a hardware device, actually, just from playing around with it and bypassing stuff.

639
00:36:51,740 --> 00:36:51,920
Awesome.

640
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:55,940
And, and, and, and, and, you know, we were just kind of talking about that.

641
00:36:56,080 --> 00:37:04,480
And I think it, that is a blessing and a curse, that propensity, that, that, you know, ability to do it right off the way, right in the beginning.

642
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:12,460
Because, you know, when you, when you have a natural knack for it and you, you know, you find some bugs right away, you have to grind a little bit less.

643
00:37:12,760 --> 00:37:22,760
And then when you go up against a target that doesn't match with your style, it becomes, it becomes very disappointing and very challenging and really destructive to your ability.

644
00:37:24,040 --> 00:37:26,420
You know, your self-perception as a hacker, right?

645
00:37:26,420 --> 00:37:44,120
And so, yeah, it's a double-edged sword, I always say to people that are kind of coming in and it's great if you've got it and it, but if you don't, you're going to learn how to, you're going to learn what hacking really looks like most of the time, which is sitting there, reading the JavaScript files, playing with the endpoints, opening 500 repeater tabs until your eyes bleed.

646
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:46,700
And then finally, you know, breaking in.

647
00:37:46,700 --> 00:37:49,160
There's always a better hacker.

648
00:37:49,420 --> 00:37:49,560
Yeah.

649
00:37:49,660 --> 00:37:56,780
And, you know, you may be super happy with the book that you found or, or you may not find a week, a book for a week or something.

650
00:37:56,780 --> 00:38:05,100
But I, I especially got this during life hacking events when you see, maybe you had a bad day or maybe the target was just not for you.

651
00:38:05,100 --> 00:38:10,580
And you see all these people making so much money on exactly the same things that you've been looking at.

652
00:38:10,580 --> 00:38:19,220
And then, you know, I just remember, I, I tried to then look at previous scoreboards and see, oh yeah, but in last events, they were way behind me.

653
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:21,740
So no, it, it, it just all evens out.

654
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:24,020
Nobody can be good at anything.

655
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:28,620
My personal technique was totally different than, than other people's technique.

656
00:38:28,620 --> 00:38:30,560
And sometimes that technique pays off.

657
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:35,260
What I would do is I would really try to first set myself on objective.

658
00:38:35,780 --> 00:38:37,420
What, what do I want to achieve?

659
00:38:37,540 --> 00:38:38,120
I'm the hacker.

660
00:38:38,300 --> 00:38:38,940
I'm the attacker.

661
00:38:38,940 --> 00:38:40,920
And like, what kind of data do I want?

662
00:38:41,300 --> 00:38:44,740
And then I would look for the most exotic ways to get there.

663
00:38:44,820 --> 00:38:57,880
Like not the standard ways where I just like, I wouldn't even test like the, the search bar for cross-site scripting, let's say doing a life hack even, because it's, even if it only takes 15 seconds, it's going to be a waste of time.

664
00:38:57,880 --> 00:39:01,860
Just making an invoice for that $3 split that you would be getting.

665
00:39:01,860 --> 00:39:02,520
Yeah, exactly.

666
00:39:03,040 --> 00:39:03,500
So.

667
00:39:04,100 --> 00:39:04,360
Yeah.

668
00:39:04,900 --> 00:39:07,060
That's a, that's a very important part.

669
00:39:07,060 --> 00:39:13,540
And of, I think, and something we've talked about as well, Joel, in the past, these, this sort of goal setting piece.

670
00:39:13,540 --> 00:39:15,540
Yeah.

671
00:39:15,540 --> 00:39:17,040
And, and I think it's core to a lot of hackers mentalities.

